# DIAGNOSTICS

fs prints why it stopped, `no partition PATH` or `no volume on PATH`, and exits 1.
A call the service doesn't do yet fails with `unsupported`.

# BUGS

There are no permissions, owners or symbolic links over Node.
Files open when fs restarts stay closed; `/data` itself reconnects to the new fs (launcher(8)).
Free space is a bitmap held in memory six times over (in use, and blocks held, deferred, retired, allocated and logged in the current groups): about 180 MB on a 1 TB partition.
A commit's work on the bitmap grows with what changed since the last, except the first after the volume is mounted, which hashes the whole bitmap (about 40 ms a terabyte on the dev machine); requests wait while a commit runs.
